//! CPython's own codec space, transcribed: the label rules, the alias table, and
//! every single-byte decoding table that `encodings` publishes.

//! This file is generated. `/tmp` sweeps the interpreter CPython 3.12.15 really runs
//! (the module files, `codecs.lookup(label).name` for every spelling, and every byte
//! of every `decoding_table` decoded strictly) and writes the answer here, so the
//! numbers in this file are the interpreter's, not transcribed from a specification.
//! Two decisions make the tables the right shape:
//!
//! * The lookup resolves a **label**, but `codecs.lookup(label).name` -- not the
//!   module name -- is what the interpreter reports and what the differential oracle
//!   freezes. So tables are keyed by canonical name, and the two modules that share
//!   a name (`iso8859_1`, `latin_1`) were swept and proved byte-identical, which is
//!   why keying by name is safe rather than lucky.
//! * Only labels whose decoder this crate can actually run are carried. A label that
//!   resolves to something else -- `utf-16`, `big5hkscs`, `punycode`, `hex` -- gets
//!   `None` from [`decode_by_label`], which is the same answer as an unknown label
//!   and the same fall-through [`super::resolve::decode_body`] does with it. `None`
//!   means "this port has no opinion", never "this byte sequence is invalid".
//!
//! Multi-byte codecs live elsewhere on purpose: `gbk` in [`super::gbk`], the
//! gb2312/big5/shift_jis/cp932 family in [`super::cjk`] -- those tables were built
//! there because Windows-ACP grids diverge from CPython's, and `utf-8` is
//! [`std::str::from_utf8`].

/// One byte -> one code point. A byte with no character is [`UNDEFINED`]; every byte
/// in a carried table was swept and maps to a single code point or to nothing, so a
/// table answer never has to guess between the two.
pub type Charmap = [u16; 256];

/// The hole marker. Safe because it is the one thing a carried table cannot hold:
/// the sweep found no byte mapping to U+FFFE and none mapping to U+FFFF.
pub const UNDEFINED: u16 = 0xFFFE;

